# Boolean variable as a condition

Verifies an `if` reads its condition from a boolean variable rather than a
literal: the body runs for the true variable and is skipped for the false one,
after which execution continues normally.

>>> source
flag: bool = true
if (flag) {
    print(1)
}

other: bool = false
if (other) {
    print(2)
}

print(3)

<<< stdout
1
3

<<< stderr
